---
source: crates/biome_html_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.svelte
---
# Input
```svelte
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<div><li /></div>
<ul>{#if visible}<div><li>Indirect child</li></div>{/if}</ul>
{#snippet item()}
    <div><li>Item in a div</li><li /></div>
{/snippet}
<div>
    {#if visible}
        <li>Conditional item</li>
    {:else if pending}
        <li>Pending item</li>
    {:else}
        <li />
    {/if}
    {#each items as item}
        <li>{item}</li>
    {/each}
    {#await promise}
        <li>Loading</li>
    {:then item}
        <li>{item}</li>
    {:catch error}
        <li>{error}</li>
    {/await}
    {#key value}
        <li />
    {/key}
</div>
<div><svelte:boundary><li>Boundary item</li></svelte:boundary></div>
<div><slot><li>Slot fallback item</li></slot></div>
<template><div><li>Item in a div</li></div></template>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.svelte:2:6 lint/nursery/noMisplacedListElements ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  × This <li> element is outside a list container.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <div><li /></div>
      │      ^^^^^^
    3 │ <ul>{#if visible}<div><li>Indirect child</li></div>{/if}</ul>
    4 │ {#snippet item()}
  
  i List items need a list container to form a valid HTML list.
  
  i Make this element a direct child of <ul>, <ol>, or <menu>.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

